// CH1 - PowerShell Downloads - BYPASSED  |  ADE1-01 Substring Manipulation
// Rule intent : catch PowerShell downloading a file.
// The bug     : the rule matches LITERAL cmdlet strings. The attacker built the same
//               download by concatenation ('Net.We'+'bClient', 'Down'+'loadFile',
//               'ht'+'tp://') so none of those literal tokens ever appear.
// Try it      : returns NOTHING on the CTF data.
ProcessCreate_CH1
| where Process has_any ("powershell.exe","powershell_ise.exe")
| where CommandLine has_any ("Net.WebClient","DownloadFile","Invoke-WebRequest","Invoke-Shellcode","http:","https:")

